# The build context is the repository root (both Dockerfiles need the
# workspace files). An allowlist: only the workspace manifests, the lockfile
# and apps/ reach the builder, minus the files below. Anything else placed
# under apps/ (a database dump, say) would still reach the build stage and its
# cache: keep such files out of the repository tree. The final images get only
# what their Dockerfiles copy.
*
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!tsconfig.base.json
!apps/

# Inside apps/: host installs, build output, logs, and secrets in their usual
# file forms stay out.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/dist-dev
**/.astro
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.log
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
**/.envrc
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.jks
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ecdsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/*.dump
apps/api/src/prisma/generated
